"Internal Error ()\nciteturn31524view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.00485v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: Failed to fetch https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.00485v1: Cache miss\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2602.00307v1] Autonomous Data Processing using Meta-Agents (https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.00307v1)\nciteturn31524view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.00307v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 163\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Artificial Intelligence\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 30 Jan 2026 (this version), latest version 19 Feb 2026 (cite5†v2 )]\nL9: # Title:Autonomous Data Processing using Meta-Agents\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Udayan Khurana L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Autonomous Data Processing using Meta-Agents, by Udayan Khurana\nL14: \nL15: cite7†View PDF cite8†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Traditional data processing pipelines are typically static and handcrafted for specific tasks, limiting their adaptability to evolving requirements. While general-purpose agents and coding assistants can generate code for well-understood data pipelines, they lack the ability to autonomously monitor, manage, and optimize an end-to-end pipeline once deployed.\nL17: We present \\textbf{Autonomous Data Processing using Meta-agents} (ADP-MA), a framework that dynamically constructs, executes, and iteratively refines data processing pipelines through hierarchical agent orchestration. At its core, \\textit{meta-agents} analyze input data and task specifications to design a multi-phase plan, instantiate specialized \\textit{ground-level agents}, and continuously evaluate pipeline performance.\nL18: The architecture comprises three key components: a planning module for strategy generation, an orchestration layer for agent coordination and tool integration, and a monitoring loop for iterative evaluation and backtracking. Unlike conventional approaches, ADP-MA emphasizes context-aware optimization, adaptive workload partitioning, and progressive sampling for scalability.\nL19: Additionally, the framework leverages a diverse set of external tools and can reuse previously designed agents, reducing redundancy and accelerating pipeline construction. We demonstrate ADP-MA through an interactive demo that showcases pipeline construction, execution monitoring, and adaptive refinement across representative data processing tasks.\nL20: Subjects:  | Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI); Databases (cs.DB); Multiagent Systems (cs.MA)\nL21: Cite as:  | cite9†arXiv:2602.00307 [cs.AI]\nL22:    | (or cite10†arXiv:2602.00307v1 [cs.AI] for this version)\nL23:    | cite11†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2602.00307†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Udayan Khurana [cite12†view email ]\nL27: [v1] Fri, 30 Jan 2026 20:58:17 UTC (3,932 KB)\nL28: cite5†[v2] Thu, 19 Feb 2026 10:12:18 UTC (87 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled Autonomous Data Processing using Meta-Agents, by Udayan Khurana\nL35: \nL36:   * cite7†View PDF L37:   * cite8†HTML (experimental) L38:   * cite13†TeX Source L39: \nL40: cite14†view license L41: ### Current browse context:\nL42: \nL43: cs.AI\nL44: \nL45: cite15†< prev |   cite16†next > L46: \nL47: cite17†new | cite18†recent | cite19†2026-02 L48: \nL49: Change to browse by:\nL50: \nL51: cite20†cs L52: cite21†cs.DB L53: cite22†cs.MA L54: \nL55: ### References & Citations\nL56: \nL57:   * cite23†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L58:   